{
  "about": "The waiting fields (amendment, Contract shapes), read by Bodies.waiting (Kotlin) and parseWaitingFields (TS). env is the build's. expected null means unreadable. Kotlin reads label..pollSeconds and skips jsOnly rows; TS also reads code, heartbeatUrl and startUrl, which only it keeps, and skips kotlinOnly rows, which are shaped as a beat's answer (capture-beat.v1 $defs.answer): only Kotlin reads those. Every other row is shaped as capture-descriptor.v1's waiting branch. A field absent or null where the schema allows it is null; a field of the wrong type, or outside the schema's bounds, makes the whole unreadable (a length counts characters, that is code points, as JSON Schema counts them); an overlayUrl off the build's Seazn host is dropped alone. A descriptor may carry an optional stage (capture-descriptor.v1, W28): expected.stageLabel is its label, shown verbatim, only when its role.kind is one of wire/stage-kinds.json and the label is 1 to 40 characters (code points); any other stage, or none, is null, and never makes the row unreadable. A beat has no stage. Change only with both.",
